terminal tile. If I keep it, it might help in patterns like All Terminals or All Honors and Terminals. But since I don't have many terminals yet, maybe it's better to discard it if it's not part of a meld. However, T1 could be part of a Chi if I get T2 and T3, but that's not likely.\n\n- Discard F4: F4 is a South Wind, which is the prevailing wind. If I can form a Pung of F4, that would give me 2 points (Prevalent Wind) and possibly other patterns. But I need two more F4. There are two left. If I discard F4, I lose that chance. So keeping F4 is better.\n\n- Discard W2: W2 is part of the existing Chi. If I discard it, there are two left. Keeping it might allow for a Pung if two more are drawn. But again, unlikely.\n\n- Discard B2: B2 is part of the existing Chi. Discarding it might not be as bad since the Chi is already formed. There's one left in the unshown. If I discard B2, someone else might discard it, and I can Peng it, but I can't do that here. So maybe it's safe to discard.\n\n- Discard W6: W6 is part of the existing Chi [W6, W7, W8]. Discarding it would leave one in hand. But there are two left in the unshown. If I discard W6, maybe someone else can use it, but it's part of a Chi already. Not sure.\n\nConsidering the need to form a fourth meld and a pair, the most flexible tile to discard might be T1 or B2. If I discard T1, I lose a terminal, but maybe it's not as valuable. If I discard B2, I lose a tile that could be part of a Pung if another B2 is drawn. But since the Chi is already formed, maybe B2 is less critical.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the best move is to discard W2. Because if I discard W2, there are still two in the unshown, and I can form a Pung if I draw two more. However, the chance is low. Alternatively, if I discard B2, there's one left, so if I draw it, I can form a Pung. But with only one left, it's also unlikely.\n\nWait, the unshown B2 has 1 left. So if I discard B2, there's only one left. If I draw it, I can form a Pung. But there's only one left. So the chance is 1 tile out of the remaining unshown. If I keep B2, I have one in hand and one in the wall. If I draw the one in the wall, I can form a Pung. So maybe keeping B2 is better than discarding it.\n\nSimilarly for W2: unshown has 2 left. So keeping W2 gives me a better chance to form a Pung if I draw two more. But again, unlikely.\n\nGiven that, perhaps the best move is to discard a tile that's not useful for any patterns. T1 is a terminal, but if I discard it, maybe it's better to keep other tiles. F4 is a wind tile, which could be useful for Prevalent Wind. So maybe discard T1 or B2.\n\nLooking at the unshown tiles, T1 has 1 left. If I discard T1, it's a terminal, which might be needed by others. But if I keep it, I can use it for All Terminals or similar. However, since I don't have enough terminals yet, maybe it's better to discard T1.\n\nAlternatively, if I discard B2, I can still form a Pung if I draw another B2. But there's only one left. So the chance is 1/remaining tiles. If I discard B2, the remaining B2 is 1. If I keep B2, then the remaining is 1, so same chance. So maybe it's better to keep B2 in hand to have it, in case I need to form a Pung.\n\nSo between T1 and B2. If I discard T1, I lose a terminal but maybe it's not part of any meld. If I discard B2, I lose a tile that could be part of a Pung. Since B2 has a chance to form a Pung (if I draw the remaining one), maybe it's better to keep B2 and discard T1.\n\nTherefore, the best action is to discard T1.\n", "output": "Evaluation: The best move is to discard T1 as it is a terminal tile with limited utility for forming additional melds and does not contribute to high-value patterns like Pungs or Kongs. Keeping other tiles like F4 (South Wind, aligning with the prevailing wind) and W2/B2 offers better chances for future melds or scoring patterns.\nReason: Discarding T1 reduces the risk of losing a terminal tile that is less critical for current melds, while preserving honor tiles (F4) and suited tiles (W2, B2) that could form Pungs or contribute to higher-point patterns like Prevalent Wind.\nAnswer: Play T1"}
